0 < 2 {
1 < 2   "version": "questions-v1",
3 > 2   "about": "Every Jev question set the Flock puts to `POST /v1/systemone` during a run. `flock_step`, read by factory/flock/step_reading.mjs once per green story step; `flock_peer_rewrite`, read by factory/flock/engine.mjs when an edit replaces a peer's lines; and `flock_peer_settled`, its second look before a draft for a line of main's read as lost. Their modes live in factory/policy.json's `flock.jev_step` and `flock.jev_peer_rewrite` (`second_look`). The authoring sets live beside their readers, in skills/ultrawrite/stories/questions.json (#1449). Each set names its reader and its rollback (map #1131 rule 3). A question is literal: it names no policy word, and nothing here decides anything. A Jev `null` routes that reading to the set's stated rollback, never to a guess. A reworded question is a different question: its readings mean something else.",
2 < 2   "about": "Every Jev question set the Flock puts to `POST /v1/systemone` during a run. `flock_step`, read by factory/flock/step_reading.mjs once per green story step; and `flock_peer_rewrite`, read by factory/flock/engine.mjs when an edit replaces a peer's lines; their modes live in factory/policy.json's `flock.jev_step` and `flock.jev_peer_rewrite`. The authoring sets live beside their readers, in skills/ultrawrite/stories/questions.json (#1449). Each set names its reader and its rollback (map #1131 rule 3). A question is literal: it names no policy word, and nothing here decides anything. A Jev `null` routes that reading to the set's stated rollback, never to a guess. A reworded question is a different question: its readings mean something else.",
3 < 2   "sets": {
