72 < 2       ],
73 < 2       "provenance": "flock-baseline run-23 (2026-11-13): a builder asked to make one file of two folded main's opening line into its own in one edit and deleted main's in the next; the peer-rewrite read saw the second edit alone and answered loses at 0.43, and the run, whose file kept everything, ended a draft. Read from the laptop, jev-latest, 2026-11-13, n=27 answers over 9 cases: run-23's file carried 3 of 3, run-17's forced loss drops 3 of 3, five more losses and rewordings as wanted; a wording that asked about the side's meaning as a whole read run-17 as carried 3 of 3 and was dropped",
74 < 2       "calibrated": false,
